1. e4 f5 2. exf5 Nf6 { The arrows indicate the variance in the different lines by white. Of course the Queen move is a blunder ;). Interesting is to see that players who play the best line d4 only use limited variations afterwards. So this is easy to anticipate. } { [%cal Gg2g4,Bf1e2,Bf1d3,Bd2d3,Rd1h5] } 3. g4 { Let's learn how black should react on the most divers response, g4. } *


